case: a pinned claim is listed as pinned: true
case: a marked claim is listed with its kind: true
case: a claim with neither pin nor marker is refused: true
case: a claim in capitals is a claim too: true
case: a pin to another mode is no pin: true
case: a marker of an unknown kind is refused: true
case: a one-word reason is refused: true
case: a sentinel that does not open its comment is refused: true
case: two markers are refused: true
case: a pin and a marker together are refused: true
case: a marker with no claim is refused: true
case: the word in a comment is no claim: true
every test source lexes: true
the walk read the arrayjit package's test sources too: true
some listed source pins the mode in-process: true
some listed source carries a marker: true
every test source claiming bitwise equality pins cc_backend_fp_contract=off or carries one well-formed marker, and every marker disposes of a claim: true

Kinds:
exact-operands -- every product and partial sum is exact at the compared precision, so a fused multiply-add rounds where the separate ones do: nowhere
no-contraction -- the compared values involve no floating product feeding an add: nothing for the compiler to fuse
same-shape -- on cc, both sides run the same kernel code, so they contract alike
gated -- the claim reads the kernel's flags and target at run time and skips where they differ
not-cc -- only a GPU backend evaluates the claim; cc skips it
not-executed -- no claim is about executed values: fixtures, codegen text, host arithmetic

Test sources whose string literals claim bitwise equality:
test/operations/autotune_grid_record.ml -- exact-operands: Ll_test.exact_partials derives the operands' sums exact at f32
test/operations/autotune_seeded_seed.ml -- not-cc: the value claims hold only where CUDA or HIP seeds or splits; cc skips them
test/operations/bf16_subnormal_storage.ml -- no-contraction: the legs copy, convert, add or halve; no product feeds an add
test/operations/branchless_select.ml -- exact-operands: selects, adds and a pool gradient multiplying dyadic weights by one
test/operations/coalesce_numerics.ml -- not-cc: the executed bitwise claims are gated on a hardware grid, so cc skips them
test/operations/codegen_text_scan_cases.ml -- not-executed: the bitwise text is fixture prose a codegen-text scan classifies
test/operations/cost_model_fill.ml -- not-executed: the bitwise claim compares cost-model scores computed in OCaml
test/operations/cost_model_transactions.ml -- not-executed: the bitwise claims compare cost-model legs computed in OCaml
test/operations/cpu_parallel.ml -- same-shape: one compiled pure-add routine runs twice and its results are compared
